Z||000025||Joe Torma||12-12-2001||12:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87GTZ34:<BR><B>Joe,<P>What are you using for the EL driver?  Also, what voltage (min - max) and freq are you driving it at?<P>TIA</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>A 12V to 100V 1600Hz inverter driver.  WHy do you ask?  They are dimmable.<P>I bet the sheets I have will probably get brighter when 14V is fed to them.<P>The new material requires a different driver...don't know the specs.<P>Thanks Nashco  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
